@0    = ~Each of you has eluded Tyr's judgement, but no longer. You are all monsters-in-flesh. The day of judgment is at hand. You are mere flies in my web, and have been invited to this island to die. First, Adrik. And soon, you.~
@1    = ~Bah! As if that is enough to intimidate a Red Wizard! Edwin Odesseiron is not so easily cowed (nor so easily killed).~
@2    = ~Calling us monsters? What a sick prank this is!~
@3    = ~Bah! Tyr's judgement? As if Tyr would approve of using a zombie like that!~
@4    = ~Well, since no one is using that body anymore... Could I have it? Please? It looks very fresh, dead for not even a few hours. Drowning has such interesting effects on a cadaver, and I so rarely get to study a drowned corpse!~
@5    = ~That's enough out of ye! Can't ye see we got bigger problems than yer research interests?!~
@6    = ~ So, this is... embarrassing to admit, but I don't actually know any Zashir Anskuln. I swear to the gods that I have never met anyone of that name in my life. Does anyone actually know our host?~
@7    = ~Anyone?~
@8    = ~No one at all?~
@9    = ~It's weird. This whole situation is strange. Honestly, I could use a drink about now.~
@10   = ~Splendid idea. Let's just-oh, Pelial, how much have you had already?! That is a simply obscene amount!~
@11   = ~(Pelial sets down another empty bottle, but something is wrong. He is pallid, with a panicked expression. His lips move, but only a choking sound comes out. Moments later, he falls from his chair and hits the ground with a sickening thud. He is dead.)~
@12   = ~Oh dear. Oh dear, oh dear. No one drink anything! This is... this is horrible!~
@13   = ~“Horrible” is an understatement. We are on a remote island, with naught much to do but wait until death finds us all, one by one.~
@14   = ~‘Twas poison! A cowardly weapon.~
@15   = ~Lucky he broke into the drinks well before we did. Er, lucky for us I mean.~
@16   = ~Horrible? Better just him than all of us. Besides, good riddance! Do you have any idea who that person really was? That was Pirate Captain Pelial.~
@17   = ~I thought he looked familiar.~
@18   = ~That scoundrel! His men robbed my husband's ship. Unless he was here to return our priceless family heirlooms, good riddance, I say!~
@19   = ~How did HE get invited here?~
@20   = ~Maybe he didn't. Wouldn't surprise me if he stole an invitation.~
@21   = ~Wait, how did you know who he was?~
@22   = ~I was on one of the ships he robbed. You never forget a guy who does that to you.~
@23   = ~Well, that's all very well and good. And good riddance to him! But Shipmaster Adrik was our way off the island, and now he's dead in front of us. ~
@24   = ~And apparently, whoever killed Adrik and Pelial wants *all* of us dead. Maybe we should focus more on living and figuring out who the killer is.~
@25   = ~What about those rowboats at the docks here?~
@26   = ~Rowboats can't get us all the way back to the Gate.~
@27   = ~Hey, <CHARNAME>, you're the Hero of Nashkel, aren't you? Can't you do something here? The murderer might be on the island.~
@28   = ~But gods, what if one of us is the murderer?!~
@29   = ~Now, there's no reason to get into hysterics.There's plenty of food in the storage huts here. All we have to do is wait a few days until Zashir arrives.~
@30   = ~In the meantime, Tremona and I can look around the island and see if there's anywhere for anyone to hide. Maybe there's some clues somewhere. <CHARNAME>, you're welcome to do the same.~
@31   = ~We should all buddy up, too. We probably shouldn't be alone, just in case.~
@32   = ~Splendid idea. I'll buddy up with Enger. Carasta, you can go with Tremona. <CHARNAME>, you stay with Drunlo. I suppose you can talk to him when you're ready to go back to your hut to sleep. ~
@33   = ~Groan...~
@34   = ~(Continue)~
@35   = ~....~
